      - c/address.mojo, c/network.mojo, c/socket.mojo, socket.mojo,
        address.mojo, connection.mojo, server.mojo, uri.mojo,
        loop/state.mojo (2026-09-29): IPv6 listening, which could not work.
        `AF_INET6` was OpenBSD's 24, which macOS refuses and Linux reads as
        `AF_PPPOX`; it is 30 on macOS and 10 on Linux. `inet_pton` returns
        every byte it wrote (`InetAddress`, sixteen for IPv6) where it read
        four back as a `c_uint`, and `inet_ntop` takes them. `SocketAddress`
        is `sockaddr_storage`-sized with a length, where one 16-byte
        `sockaddr` truncated an IPv6 address, and `sockaddr_host_port` is
        the one reader of an address the kernel filled -- `accept_with_peer`,
